    <h4>2. About Wawe Journal</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal is a trading journal and performance analytics platform designed to help users record, organize, sync and analyze their trading activity.</p>
    <p>Depending on the features available to the user, the platform may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Manual trade logging and trade history management.</li><li>Syncing of existing trades from supported broker accounts.</li><li>Trading statistics, profit and loss calculations, win rate, risk/reward ratios and performance analytics.</li><li>Creating, documenting and analyzing trading strategies.</li><li>Simulations of prop firm evaluation processes and trading rules.</li><li>AI-assisted trade analyses and reviews, once made available.</li><li>Backtesting and hypothetical strategy evaluations.</li></ul>
    <p>Wawe Journal is designed for keeping and analyzing trading records. The availability of features may depend on the user's subscription, account configuration and the features released on the platform.</p>
    <h4>3. No Financial or Investment Advice</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal does not provide personalized investment advice, financial planning, or recommendations to buy, sell or hold any financial instrument.</p>
    <p>All information, statistics, reports, charts, strategy evaluations, simulations and other outputs generated by the platform are provided for informational and educational purposes only.</p>
    <p>No content on the platform should be interpreted as a guarantee of profitability, a trading recommendation, or a substitute for independent financial assessment.</p>
    <p>Users are solely responsible for their trading decisions and for any profits or losses that may result from them.</p>
    <h4>4. Trading Journal and Performance Analytics</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal provides tools for users to record, organize, track and analyze their trading activity.</p>
    <p>Performance metrics may include trade history, profit and loss results, win rate, average wins and losses, risk/reward ratios, drawdown measurements and other statistical indicators.</p>
    <p>The accuracy of these metrics depends on the completeness and accuracy of the underlying data, the calculation methods used and the availability of the relevant information.</p>
    <p>While reasonable care is taken to provide reliable calculations and analysis tools, no result is guaranteed to be complete, accurate, uninterrupted or error-free.</p>
    <p>Users should independently verify important financial calculations and, where necessary, compare synced trade records with their broker's official account statements.</p>
    <h4>5. Broker Connections and Read-Only Access</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal may allow users to connect supported broker accounts via API or other supported authentication and authorization methods.</p>
    <p>These connections are used to retrieve and sync existing trade records for journaling, reporting and analysis purposes.</p>
    <p><strong>Wawe Journal is designed to have read-only access to broker data. The platform does not execute trades on the user's behalf, open or close positions, place or modify orders, withdraw funds, or manage users' broker accounts.</strong></p>
    <p>The platform's access is limited to the data and permissions made available through the supported connection method.</p>
    <p>Users should review the permissions requested when connecting their accounts. Actual access permissions depend on the respective broker and the authentication or authorization method used.</p>
    <p>Broker APIs and third-party services may change, become unavailable, or provide incomplete or delayed information. Sync errors, data discrepancies, missing records and other technical issues may occur.</p>
    <p>Users are responsible for reviewing synced trade records and confirming the accuracy of important information against their broker's official account statements.</p>
    <p>Connecting a broker account does not transfer ownership or control of that account to Wawe Journal.</p>
    <h4>6. Data Collection, Processing and Storage</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal may collect, process, transfer and store information related to user accounts and trading activity in order to provide its journaling and analytics features.</p>
    <p>Depending on the features used, trading data may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Trade history.</li><li>Financial instrument symbols.</li><li>Buy and sell direction, including long and short position information.</li><li>Entry and exit prices.</li><li>Position size or lot amount.</li><li>Trade timestamps and related time information.</li><li>Performance metrics and analytics data derived from trade records.</li></ul>
    <p>Information may be entered manually by users or retrieved through supported broker integrations.</p>
    <p>Synced trade records are transferred to and stored on Wawe Journal's infrastructure in order to provide the platform's features.</p>
    <p>Wawe Journal uses infrastructure and services provided by Cloudflare and Supabase to support the operation of the application, data storage, authentication-related functions, security controls and performance.</p>
    <p>The exact location where data is processed may depend on the infrastructure used, the service configuration and the architecture of these providers. Wawe Journal does not claim that all data is stored in a single physical location or that data necessarily remains within the borders of a particular country.</p>
    <p>Data may be processed on infrastructure distributed across multiple locations, depending on the relevant service configuration and the providers' practices.</p>
    <p>More detailed information on the processing of personal data, service providers and applicable privacy rights is available in the Wawe Journal <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    <h4>7. Data Retention and Account Deletion</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal retains users' stored trade records and associated account data until the user requests deletion or deletes the relevant information through the available account features.</p>
    <p>Following a deletion request, the relevant data is deleted from active systems in accordance with applicable deletion procedures.</p>
    <p>Where necessary, some information may be temporarily retained in backups, security logs or other systems. Such data is kept only for legitimate operational, security or legal purposes and to the extent permitted by applicable law and the relevant retention policies.</p>
    <p>Where applicable, users may contact Wawe Journal for assistance with deleting their account or data.</p>
    <p>Details of the deletion process and any exceptions are described in the platform's <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and the applicable <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    <h4>8. Data Security</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal uses infrastructure and security features provided by Cloudflare and Supabase to help protect its systems and stored information.</p>
    <p>Depending on the services and configuration used, these measures may include authentication and authorization controls, network protections, access restrictions and other security mechanisms.</p>
    <p>Wawe Journal applies an authentication and authorization approach intended to ensure that only authorized users and services can access accounts and data. Additional technical information about the authentication system may be provided in the platform's technical documentation or security guide.</p>
    <p>No website, application, database, network or cloud infrastructure can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
    <p>Despite reasonable security measures, unauthorized access, data loss, service interruptions, vulnerabilities and other security incidents may occur.</p>
    <p>Wawe Journal does not guarantee absolute security or uninterrupted availability. Users should keep their account credentials secure and report any suspected unauthorized access without delay.</p>
    <h4>9. Service Continuity and Third-Party Providers</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal relies on third-party infrastructure and service providers, including Cloudflare and Supabase, to support the operation of the platform.</p>
    <p>The availability and performance of the platform may depend on these providers, network connectivity, software systems, maintenance work and other technical factors.</p>
    <p>Although distributed infrastructure and security mechanisms may be used to improve service resilience and availability, uninterrupted service cannot be guaranteed.</p>
    <p>Outages, maintenance, API changes, provider-related incidents, network failures or other conditions may temporarily affect access to the platform or the accuracy and timeliness of synced information.</p>
    <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Wawe Journal cannot be held responsible for disruptions caused by third-party services.</p>
    <h4>10. AI-Assisted Analysis</h4>
    <p>Once made available, Wawe Journal may provide AI features that analyze trade records, identify potential patterns, summarize performance or offer evaluations of strategies.</p>
    <p>AI-generated results may contain incomplete, inaccurate or misleading information, or information that is not suitable for a particular trading situation.</p>
    <p>These outputs are provided for informational and educational purposes only. They do not constitute personalized investment advice and should not be relied upon on their own when making trading or financial decisions.</p>
    <p>AI analyses do not guarantee better trading performance, fewer losses or future profitability.</p>
    <p>Users should independently evaluate AI-generated results and verify important information before acting on them.</p>
    <h4>11. Backtesting and Hypothetical Performance</h4>
    <p>Backtesting and hypothetical performance features may evaluate trading strategies using historical data, user-defined parameters or simulated market conditions.</p>
    <p>Hypothetical results have inherent limitations and do not represent actual trading performance.</p>
    <p>Historical or simulated results may not fully account for the following factors:</p>
    <ul><li>Slippage and order execution delays.</li><li>Spreads, commissions and other trading costs.</li><li>Liquidity constraints.</li><li>Market volatility and changing market conditions.</li><li>Order execution limitations.</li><li>Psychological factors and real trading behavior.</li><li>Errors, gaps or limitations in historical data.</li></ul>
    <p>Backtest results may benefit from hindsight. They may also be misleading due to overfitting, data selection, or assumptions that do not hold in real markets.</p>
    <p>Actual results may differ significantly from simulated or historical results. There is no guarantee that a strategy will achieve results similar to its backtest results.</p>
    <h4>12. Prop Firm Simulations</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal may offer simulation tools that help users review their trading activity against the rules of certain proprietary trading firms (prop firms) or hypothetical evaluation conditions.</p>
    <p>These tools may simulate profit targets, drawdown limits, daily loss limits, account rules and other evaluation parameters.</p>
    <p>Prop firm simulations are provided for practice, planning and educational purposes only.</p>
    <p>A simulation is not an official evaluation conducted by the relevant prop firm. It does not represent a real funded account, a certification, or a guarantee that the user will pass an evaluation or receive funding.</p>
    <p>Simulation results may differ from the actual rules, calculation methods, monitoring systems and decisions of the relevant firms. Rules may change over time and their interpretation may vary from firm to firm.</p>
    <p>Users should verify the applicable rules directly with the relevant prop firm.</p>
    <p>Wawe Journal does not guarantee that users will pass any evaluation, receive funding or achieve any particular trading outcome.</p>
    <h4>13. Trading Strategies and Strategy Analysis</h4>
    <p>Wawe Journal may allow users to create, document, edit and analyze trading strategies.</p>
    <p>Strategy analyses are based on the information and parameters available on the platform and may not reflect all relevant market conditions or risks.</p>
    <p>Analysis results should not be interpreted as a recommendation to use a strategy or as evidence that a strategy will be profitable in the future.</p>
    <p>Users are solely responsible for evaluating their strategies and deciding whether to use them.</p>
